EmailTemplate.textOnly:
Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

ASU encourages all students to apply for financial aid by completing the Free Application for Federal Student Aid at fafsa.ed.gov starting October 1. As an admitted student ASU will review your FAFSA to determine your eligibility for multiple types of need-based aid, see details here: students.asu.edu/financialaid/types. You will receive a Financial Aid Notification (FAN) and be able to see your financial aid package on your My ASU page under the Finances tab.

Be sure to use our cost calculators and budget worksheet, found at students.asu.edu/financialaid/tools, to determine what aid you would like to accept fully, partially, or decline based on your estimated cost of attendance.

Contact Financial Aid and Scholarship Services with further questions at 480-965-3355 or online at students.asu.edu/financialaid.

I also encourage you to look through our scholarship website, which can be found at students.asu.edu/scholarships. ASU has a scholarship portal to help you bookmark different scholarships and manage your applications and recommendation letters.

Sincerely,

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}

If you have any additional information or questions related to this, please reply to this email.

{!Case.Thread_Id}
